Name of Experiment: Write a program to implement Round Robin Algorithm.
Problem Statement: Write a program in C to implement Round Robin Scheduling algorithms
Software /Hardware Requirements: Turbo C++ Compiler, Personal Computer
Theory:
Round Robin (RR) is a preemptive CPU scheduling algorithm where each process is assigned a fixed 
time slot (Time Quantum) in a cyclic manner.
It is one of the simplest and most widely used scheduling techniques, especially in time-sharing 
systems.
Working Principle:
1. All processes are kept in a ready queue.
2. CPU picks the first process and gives it the CPU for a fixed time quantum.
3. If the process finishes within the time, it is removed from the queue.
4. If it does not finish, it is preempted and placed at the back of the queue with its remaining 
5. burst time.
6. This cycle repeats until all processes are completed.
Key Terms:
 Time Quantum (TQ):
The fixed time period a process can execute before being preempted.
 Context Switching:
Saving and loading the state of a process when switching between processes.
Formulas:
 Turnaround Time (TAT) = Completion Time – Arrival Time
 Waiting Time (WT) = Turnaround Time – Burst Time
